    "notes": [
      "Opening fact (f001) is the visit reason from opening_scenario (pre-employment checkup) because the chief-complaint answer is 'No.'; that 'No' is kept as an absent fact (f002), even though he goes on to report a chronic cough.",
      "Polarity warning on 'cc' (v1 absent, v2 absent + present) is expected: v1 keeps the visit reason as opening_fact with source 'cc' outside patient_facts, while v2 needs it as a present fact (f001) for the opening; f001 cites 'cc' as v1's opening_fact does, and has no quote because its wording comes from opening_scenario.",
      "Questions that ask about 'recently or in the past' (p001, p002) are kept as one absent fact each, with the time span in the text and time current.",
      "p010 and p011 say the same thing and are merged (f005).",
      "Mixed-item denials (p003, p005, p007, p019, p024, p025, p027) are split into one absent fact per item.",
      "Coal-mine work is recorded as a past occupational exposure (f048, habit_exposure); its duration is unknown. Applying for a new job is the current occupation fact (f054).",
      "GERD and asthma come from a single sentence in gold_additional_diagnosis and get one record each with the same note.",
      "Conversion: v1 merged p008 and p009 into one cough fact; in v2 the several-year history is the onset child f004 of cough f003, so the duration still stays with the cough.",
      "Conversion: sputum (f008) is its own parent with amount, color and smell children; blood in sputum (f012) is a separate fact so 'coughing up blood' questions match it directly. The note-only 'no recent change' is the course child f006.",
      "Conversion: v1 f049 (a pack a day for 10 years) becomes smoking f051 with quantity (f052) and duration (f053) children; the vaccination papers (v1 f044) are a child of vaccinations (f042).",
